@startuml pathmap-cow-share
' ============================================================================
' pathmap-cow-share.puml — persistent copy-on-write: two versions share nodes.
' Replaces the ASCII structural-sharing figure in
' docs/algorithms/implementations/pathmap-dictionary.md.
' Adding "test" to {best, rest}: only the new 't' branch is allocated; the
' 'b'/'r' branch and the 'est' suffix are reused. Both roots stay valid.
' Color key:  grey = version roots   teal = shared (reused) nodes   green = the new node
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #212121
  BorderThickness 1.1
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #B2DFDB
skinparam noteBorderColor #00796B
skinparam TitleFontSize 15

title Persistent COW — adding "test" to { "best", "rest" } keeps both versions

rectangle "**root₁**\nVersion 1" as R1 #ECEFF1
rectangle "**root₂**\nVersion 2  (+ “test”)" as R2 #ECEFF1
rectangle "'b' / 'r'\nbranch" as BR #B2DFDB
rectangle "'t'\n(new)" as T #C8E6C9
rectangle "'est'\nshared suffix" as EST #B2DFDB

R1 --> BR
R2 --> BR
R2 --> T
BR --> EST
T --> EST

note right of EST : Shared nodes — reused, not copied.\nBoth versions coexist.
@enduml
